__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
coverage/

# AW_WORKSPACE_HOME=/opt/aw-workspace/.aw-workspace (see Dockerfile) and
# repos/ below also live inside this repo's working tree — none of it is
# project source, it's runtime state that happens to sit under the same path.
/repos/
/apps/*
!/apps/README.md
/.*/
# ...except .github, which is real project source (CI workflows). A negation
# can only re-include a path whose PARENT directory isn't excluded, so the
# directory has to be un-ignored here, before any rule below tries to name a
# file inside it. Without this, `/.*/` above silently swallows every NEW file
# under .github/ — the existing workflows only survive because they were
# already tracked, and git never re-evaluates ignores for tracked files.
!/.github/

# --- Agent-facing generated state (aw-workspace-cli agent sync) --------------
# native-skills/ is the source of truth for the skills THIS repo owns. Every
# directory below is generated and must never be committed or hand-edited:
#
#   skills/      merge of native-skills/ + every installed app's
#                contributes.skills. It is what agents and containers actually
#                read (Codex reads it raw, the kb app's load_skill reads it
#                raw, and app containers bind-mount it), so it has to hold
#                everything — but nothing in it is authored here.
#   .claude/ …   per-CLI mirrors of skills/, one copy per agent CLI.
#
# skills/ holds app-contributed skills that only exist once their app is
# installed, so committing it would put a workspace's app roster into this
# repo's history. (The `/.*/` rule above already hides the dot-dirs, but
# they're named explicitly so the intent survives a change to that catch-all.)
/skills/
.claude/
.cursor/
.gemini/

# Per-CLI mirrors of AGENTS.md — generated, not hand-edited. Edit AGENTS.md.
# Note copilot-instructions.md sits INSIDE the just-un-ignored .github/, so it
# needs its own rule — it's the one file there that isn't project source.
CLAUDE.md
GEMINI.md
/.github/copilot-instructions.md

# Playwright MCP scratch output
.playwright-mcp/

# Root dot-FILES. The `/.*/` rule above only covers dot-directories, so these
# sat untracked-but-not-ignored — which meant `git status` showed credentials
# as pending work and a `git add -A` would have committed them. Found
# 2026-08-14: .git-credentials (a GitHub token) and .bash_history were both
# sitting there, and .mcp.json carries the MCP gateway bearer token that
# installed apps write into it at boot.
/.git-credentials
/.gitconfig
/.bash_history
/.claude.json
/.mcp.json
/.cgcignore
